course: dictionary
lesson: 5785
title: Meet the lynx
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lynx is a wild cat of medium size. Its clues are tufts of black fur on the tips of its ears, a short tail and big furry paws. When you see these words near a name, you can picture the animal.
explain: Read this: «The Eurasian lynx has big furry snowshoe paws, a short stubby tail and two black ear tufts.» Those words around lynx tell you what it looks like. Ask yourself what the words describe, and you will understand more.
explain: Lynx is a noun, so it names a thing. It can be singular or plural: one lynx, two lynx or two lynxes. Writers often add clues about where an animal lives and what it eats, so look for those too.
fact: A lynx is a wild cat of medium size.
fact: A lynx has tufts of black fur on the tips of its ears, a short tail and big furry paws.
fact: Lynx live in forests of North America, Europe and Asia.
fact: «Lynx» can be one lynx or two lynxes, and it is also used for more than one lynx: two lynx.
fact: «Lynx» are rare and protected in parts of Ukraine, where they hunt hares and roe deer.
exercise: «The Eurasian lynx has a short stubby tail and two black ear tufts.» What is a lynx? | A bird | A kind of tree | A wild dog | *A wild cat
exercise: «Lynx are shy wild cats that eat deer and are not known to attack people.» What does shy mean here? | *Keeps away and does not like to be seen | Hungry for people | Very loud and bold | Brightly coloured
exercise: Where do lynx live? | In deserts of Africa | In the cities of Australia | *In forests of North America, Europe and Asia | In the open sea
test: The text says «Wolves, elk, deer, wild boar, lynx, foxes and even brown bears now live in the zone.» Which animal from this list is a wild cat? | Wolf | Elk | *Lynx | Wild boar
test: What does the word tufts mean in «two black ear tufts»? | Wet mud | Long, thin tails | Sharp claws | *Small bunches of hair or fur
exam: Ella reads «The lynx has big furry paws and a short tail» and says a lynx is a kind of bird. Which is right? | A lynx is a plant | A lynx is a kind of fish | Yes, a lynx is a bird | *A lynx is a wild cat
